## 2. Plugin registry

Registry records should include:

```ts
type PluginRelease = {
  id: string;                  // e.g. com.acme.financial-export
  version: string;             // SemVer
  digest: string;              // sha256:...
  manifest: PluginManifest;
  publisher: string;           // team/service identity
  signature: Signature;
  sbomDigest: string;
  publishedAt: string;
  status: "draft" | "approved" | "active" | "deprecated" | "revoked";
  rollout: {
    scope: "global" | "tenant" | "workspace";
    percentage?: number;
    allowlist?: string[];
  };
  securityReview: {
    approvedCapabilities: string[];
    reviewedAt: string;
    reviewer: string;
  };
};
```

Rules:

- Plugin IDs use reverse-DNS names and are permanently owned by a team.
- Only approved, signed releases can be activated.
- Registry admission validates manifest schema, signatures, SBOM, malware/dependency scans, requested capabilities, and API compatibility.
- Resolver chooses the highest non-revoked compatible version unless a tenant/report pins a version.
- A resolved plugin set is saved with each report job for reproducibility.
- Dependency resolution produces a lockfile-like result, including exact version and digest.

```json
{
  "reportJobId": "rpt_123",
  "plugins": [
    {
      "id": "com.acme.financial-export",
      "version": "2.3.1",
      "digest": "sha256:…"
    }
  ]
}
